            "review_title": "Review at Nari",
            "review_text": "caipirina\nColombo, Sri Lanka747 contributions\n0\nVery average and expensive\nNov 2014 • Family\nAround the Japanese Embassy and Kim Ma there are lots and lots of Japanese restaurants and we followed an advert in a local Japanese magazine to try Nari, specializing on meaty steak dishes. \n\nUnfortunately our experience was very average at best. The decor looks a bit tired, the partitioning of the rooms could be used greatly to create smoking and non-smoking areas, but, alas, people smoking at the tables is very typical for Japanese eateries. \n\nAs for the food, beef is pricy in Vietnam and can be hit and miss, this is how we felt like here as well. Our ten your old asked after he had finished his meal if he could have more food when we get back home! The small salad garnish could use a sprinkle of dressing, the soup arrived lukewarm ... overall, for that money you can get more and better in the area, actually, I just realized that for the 220K you can get a 2 course fine dining lunch (240 for 3 course) at a very nice place by the West Lake.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten November 1, 2014",
